{"id": "unknown-2026-09-22-006", "date": "2026-09-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Nylon filament yarn prices still elevated: What is next?", "content": "China’s nylon filament yarn prices extended their upward run, supported by firm upstream benzene and caprolactam markets.\nDownstream weaving mills bought cautiously for immediate requirements, while producers held offers firm and limited negotiation.\nIn four weeks, DTY grades rose 9.4 per cent and 9.7 per cent; FDY gained 11.9 per cent and POY led with 12.4 per cent, as latest pace eased.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/nylon-filament-yarn-prices-still-elevated-what-is-next--313676-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-22-007", "date": "2026-09-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["improve", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "India's jute sales seen rising 15% this fiscal as fibre costs ease", "content": "India’s jute sales volumes are seen rising about 15 per cent this fiscal after two weak years, helped by softer raw jute prices and a demand rebound.\nDomestic market contributes nearly 85 per cent of industry revenue and demand is projected to rise about 20 per cent.\nCrisil Ratings expects margins near 9 per cent and credit metrics to improve.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-jute-sales-seen-rising-15-this-fiscal-as-fibre-costs-ease-313672-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-22-008", "date": "2026-09-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.67, "keywords": ["loss", "weak", "uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton rebounds strongly after six-session losing streak", "content": "December 2026 ICE cotton settled 2.80 per cent higher at 83.42 cents per pound after six sessions of losses.\nChina’s State Reserve buying, broader commodity strength and China-US developments supported the rebound.\nWeak US export demand, advancing harvest activity and drought-hit crop uncertainty kept expectations of a sustained reversal limited.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-rebounds-strongly-after-six-session-losing-streak-313669-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-22-009", "date": "2026-09-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Gulf supply shock reshapes Asia polyester: Why are prices splitting?", "content": "MEG CFR China jumped 8.72 per cent to $810/mt after the Saudi pipeline drone strike, then settled at $765/mt on Friday.\nParaxylene fell about 4 per cent in Korea and Taiwan; PTA split as CFR India rose 6.67 per cent and CFR FE Asia fell 4.17 per cent.\nSaudi rerouting, China MEG restarts and futures selling capped gains, while Diwali stocking and rupee weakness kept India PTA at a premium.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/gulf-supply-shock-reshapes-asia-polyester-why-are-prices-splitting--313663-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-22-010", "date": "2026-09-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Pearl Global commissions new garment manufacturing unit in Bangladesh", "content": "Pearl Global Industries has commissioned a new garment facility and expanded sustainable laundry capacity in Bangladesh. \nThe unit adds about 7 million pieces of annual garment capacity, taking total installed capacity to about 108 million pieces per annum. \nThe laundry expansion is expected to improve efficiency, reduce washing costs and water use, and generate ROCE of about 18-20 per cent. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/pearl-global-commissions-new-garment-manufacturing-unit-in-bangladesh-313681-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
